# Build artifacts — anchored: an unanchored build/ swallowed the unrelated
# .claude/skills/build/ directory (L24)
/build/
android/**/build/
rust/target/
# The vendored dialer builds standalone for its own test lane, and an anchored
# `rust/target/` does not reach a target dir nested under `rust/vendor/` (L24 is
# the same scar from the other direction). The lane sets CARGO_TARGET_DIR out of
# the tree anyway; this is the belt to that braces, because a stray target/ here
# would be committed INTO the verbatim vendored copy.
rust/vendor/**/target/
.dart_tool/
.gradle/
*.apk
*.aab
dist/

# Generated bindings (regenerate via flutter_rust_bridge_codegen)
# lib/src/rust/ is committed for reviewability — never hand-edited

# Secrets & local environment — NEVER committed (INV-3, INV-11)
*.keystore
*.jks
key.properties
docs/environment.local.md
.env*

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store

# Flutter
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.packages
pubspec.lock.bak

# Engineering record + AI workflow — local only, versioned in the private ops
# mirror (D-047, widened to the whole tree by D-102). The public repo carries the
# product; the record behind it is internal and goes to auditors as a whole.
#
# THE MARKERS BELOW ARE LOAD-BEARING. tools/gate.sh reads the entries between them
# as the definition of the boundary — both for `internal-record boundary` (nothing
# internal is tracked here) and `internal-record pointers` (nothing tracked here
# points AT it). Until run 2 the gate hand-copied this list, so a router file added
# beside CLAUDE.md — a real near-term intent, AGENTS.md — would have been ignored
# here and unchecked there, which is the half-enforced state D-102 replaced D-047
# to end (S4-54). Add an internal path ONCE, here, and both checks widen with it.
# gate:internal-record-begin
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
docs/
# gate:internal-record-end

# Golden-diff debris from an opt-in `KV_PREVIEW=1` render. Regenerable, binary,
# and outside the gate (preview tests skip unless requested) — so an `add -A` at
# a wrap would commit it into `main` unnoticed (`dependency-steward`, UX-R2B).
test/preview/failures/
